   "subject": "rug uses bl default in ggplot but not qplot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">Hi All,<br><br>I did a histogram with a rug in ggplot, and it worked fine:<br></pre></span><br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">mydata &lt;- data.frame(x=rnorm(100))<br><br></span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">ggplot(mydata, aes(x)) +\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">geom_histogram() +\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">geom_rug()\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use &#39;binwidth = x&#39; to adjust this.</span></pre></span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"><br></span>Then I did it using qplot and it said &quot;sides&quot; has no default value. The help file says it&#39;s &quot;bl&quot;.<span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"><br><br></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">qplot(mydata$x, geom = c(&quot;histogram&quot;, &quot;rug&quot;) )\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use &#39;binwidth = x&#39; to adjust this.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error: argument &quot;sides&quot; is missing, with no default</span></pre></span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"></span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">When I specify &quot;bl&quot; it works: <br></pre></span><br></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">qplot(mydata$x, geom = c(&quot;histogram&quot;, &quot;rug&quot;), sides = &quot;bl&quot; )\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use &#39;binwidth = x&#39; to adjust this.</span></pre></span><br><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">Is this a bug, or am I misunderstanding the code differences between ggplot and qplot?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Bob<br></pre></span></span></pre></span><br><br>&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">sessionInfo()\r\n</span>R version 3.1.0 (2014-04-10)\r\nPlatform: i386-w64-mingw32/i386 (32-bit)\r\n\r\nlocale:\r\n[1] LC_COLLATE=English_United States.1252  LC_CTYPE=English_United States.1252   \r\n[3] LC_MONETARY=English_United States.1252 LC_NUMERIC=C                          \r\n[5] LC_TIME=English_United States.1252    \r\n\r\nattached base packages:\r\n[1] grid      stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     \r\n\r\nother attached packages:\r\n[1] mapproj_1.2-2 maps_2.3-6    ggplot2_1.0.0 GGally_0.4.6 \r\n\r\nloaded via a namespace (and not attached):\r\n [1] colorspace_1.2-4 digest_0.6.4     gtable_0.1.2     labeling_0.2     MASS_7.3-31     \r\n [6] munsell_0.4.2    plyr_1.8.1       proto_0.3-10     Rcpp_0.11.1      reshape_0.8.5   \r\n[11] reshape2_1.4     scales_0.2.4     stringr_0.6.2    tools_3.1.0  </pre></span><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
