   "subject": "Re: rug uses bl default in ggplot but not qplot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Dennis, that makes sense. I, too, avoid qplot as switching between the two just creates confusion unless you do it every day. However, before I realized that, I put a variation of this example in R for SAS and SPSS Users so I wanted to bring it up to date.<br><br>Cheers,<br>Bob</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br>On Saturday, May 31, 2014 3:37:58 PM UTC-4, Bob Muenchen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">Hi All,<br><br>I did a histogram with a rug in ggplot, and it worked fine:<br></pre></span><br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">mydata &lt;- data.frame(x=rnorm(100))<br><br></span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">ggplot(mydata, aes(x)) +\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">geom_histogram() +\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">geom_rug()\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">stat_bin: binwidth defaulted to range/30. Use &#39;binwidth = x&#39; to adjust this.</span></pre></span><span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"><br></span>Then I did it using qplot and it said &quot;sides&quot; has no default value. The help file says it&#39;s &quot;bl&quot;.<span style=\"white-space:pre;color:blue\"><br><br></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:19px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;bord